Gliff Android is an independent Android client for omacom/gliff, not an official
Omarchy or Samsung product.

Protocol reference:
https://github.com/omacom/gliff
Reference commit: 32bb0622cf2feef69515bf8f75a836f657f06083
Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin McConnell. MIT license, reproduced in LICENSE.
The wire-format golden tests come from crates/gliff-proto/src/msg.rs.
No upstream Rust binaries, GTK libraries, or OpenH264 binaries ship in this APK.
Video decoding uses Android MediaCodec.

Runtime libraries:
- mwiede/JSch: BSD-style license (JCraft), including its jBCrypt component.
- Bouncy Castle: MIT license.
- Jackson Core and Jackson CBOR: Apache License 2.0.

Full third-party license text is included in the APK assets/licenses directory.
